WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.458
<b>In the previous verse,</b>

2
00:00:31.458 --> 00:00:35.250
<b>Krishna explained that a practitioner </b>
<b>of Nishkama Karma Yoga</b>

3
00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:40.125
<b>becomes free from the consequences </b>
<b>of both good and bad actions in this very life.</b>

4
00:00:40.125 --> 00:00:45.208
<b>Here, He reveals what such </b>
<b>a person attains after this life.</b>

5
00:00:45.208 --> 00:00:46.875
<b>By renouncing the fruits of actions,</b>

6
00:00:46.875 --> 00:00:48.666
<b>a practitioner of selfless action</b>

7
00:00:48.666 --> 00:00:56.000
<b>ultimately achieves the supreme state </b>
<b>of liberation from the bonds of birth and death.</b>

8
00:01:00.916 --> 00:01:02.291
<b>In these verses,</b>

9
00:01:02.291 --> 00:01:08.500
<b>particularly in their translations, you </b>
<b>might encounter the term 'Buddhi Yoga'.</b>

10
00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:12.291
<b>Buddhi Yoga means using one's intellect</b>

11
00:01:12.291 --> 00:01:16.000
<b>to remain detached from </b>
<b>the fruits of one's actions,</b>

12
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.375
<b>renouncing desire for results.</b>

13
00:01:18.375 --> 00:01:22.375
<b>"Buddhi Yoga" is essentially the same as </b>
<b>"Nishkama Karma Yoga". </b>

14
00:01:22.375 --> 00:01:24.958
<b>Consider them identical.</b>

15
00:01:24.958 --> 00:01:28.333
<b>When one acts without desire for results,</b>

16
00:01:28.333 --> 00:01:35.125
<b>it signifies complete mastery over the mind.</b>

17
00:01:35.125 --> 00:01:42.583
<b>For it is the mind that houses</b>
<b>countless desires and aspirations.</b>

18
00:01:42.583 --> 00:01:46.125
<b>A practitioner of Nishkama Karma Yoga </b>
<b>has control over their mind,</b>

19
00:01:46.125 --> 00:01:52.791
<b>renouncing desires to focus</b>
<b>entirely on action without bondage.</b>

20
00:01:52.791 --> 00:01:56.750
<b>Through this practice, one becomes</b>
<b>free from the bondage of karma.</b>

21
00:01:56.750 --> 00:02:01.958
<b>Karmic bondage means being bound </b>
<b>by both good and bad consequences of actions,</b>

22
00:02:01.958 --> 00:02:08.166
<b>which keeps a soul trapped in the </b>
<b>continuous cycle of birth and death.</b>

23
00:02:08.166 --> 00:02:08.916
<b>However,</b>

24
00:02:08.916 --> 00:02:12.375
<b>by renouncing all desire for results </b>
<b>while fulfilling one's sacred duties,</b>

25
00:02:12.375 --> 00:02:19.500
<b>a practitioner of Nishkama Karma Yoga</b>
<b>breaks free from this cycle of life and death.</b>

26
00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:23.750
<b>Such a soul no longer needs to take rebirth.</b>

27
00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:24.583
<b>Perhaps</b>

28
00:02:24.583 --> 00:02:27.625
<b>a question arises in your mind here</b>

29
00:02:27.625 --> 00:02:30.833
<b>and this addresses a crucial concept</b>

30
00:02:30.833 --> 00:02:34.500
<b>while it's understandable that liberation </b>
<b>isn't achieved through negative actions,</b>

31
00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:40.000
<b>shouldn't one attain liberation</b>
<b>by performing only good actions?</b>

32
00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:41.833
<b>Following this notion,</b>

33
00:02:41.833 --> 00:02:48.958
<b>many people engage in so-called </b>
<b>good deeds with an intense desire for liberation...</b>

34
00:02:48.958 --> 00:02:49.666
<b>But</b>

35
00:02:49.666 --> 00:02:57.916
<b>what they consider good actions are actually </b>
<b>performed with expectations of positive results</b>

36
00:02:57.916 --> 00:03:00.208
<b>they expect liberation.</b>

37
00:03:00.208 --> 00:03:01.708
<b>And if this is so,</b>

38
00:03:01.708 --> 00:03:07.291
<b>doesn't it mean they're </b>
<b>still bound by expectation?</b>

39
00:03:07.291 --> 00:03:10.625
<b>And if bound, how can they be free?</b>

40
00:03:10.625 --> 00:03:12.166
<b>Where is liberation?</b>

41
00:03:12.166 --> 00:03:15.125
<b>One who remains bound by </b>
<b>the attachment to results</b>

42
00:03:15.125 --> 00:03:19.291
<b>must revolve in the cycle of birth and death.</b>

43
00:03:19.291 --> 00:03:22.666
<b>But one who rises above the</b>
<b>very expectation of results</b>

44
00:03:22.666 --> 00:03:25.916
<b>isn't that true liberation?</b>

45
00:03:25.916 --> 00:03:32.291
<b>This is why Nishkama Karma Yoga is capable</b>
<b>of liberating the soul from bondage.</b>

46
00:03:32.291 --> 00:03:33.833
<b>Now a question arises:</b>

47
00:03:33.833 --> 00:03:38.500
<b>where does the soul go after liberation?</b>

48
00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:41.000
<b>This is described in later chapters.</b>

49
00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:43.000
<b>For now, know this:</b>

50
00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:50.083
<b>a liberated soul becomes free from </b>
<b>all forms of pain and suffering.</b>

51
00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.708
<b>Humans</b>

52
00:03:56.708 --> 00:04:01.166
<b>constantly seek happiness and joy.</b>

53
00:04:01.166 --> 00:04:06.583
<b>They work endlessly to earn wealth,</b>

54
00:04:06.583 --> 00:04:11.166
<b>to acquire means of pleasure and happiness.</b>

55
00:04:11.166 --> 00:04:11.916
<b>Yet</b>

56
00:04:11.916 --> 00:04:15.208
<b>even after acquiring all these,</b>

57
00:04:15.208 --> 00:04:21.000
<b>do they remain happy and joyful?</b>

58
00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.791
<b>If material means alone could bring happiness,</b>

59
00:04:23.791 --> 00:04:28.000
<b>then every wealthy person </b>
<b>would be perpetually happy.</b>

60
00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.166
<b>And you know this </b>

61
00:04:30.166 --> 00:04:33.291
<b>isn't true.</b>

62
00:04:33.291 --> 00:04:37.375
<b>What brings joy today</b>

63
00:04:37.375 --> 00:04:42.666
<b>becomes a source of discontent tomorrow</b>
<b>when something better appears.</b>

64
00:04:42.666 --> 00:04:46.833
<b>The wealth that brings joy in its presence today</b>

65
00:04:46.833 --> 00:04:51.500
<b>will cause sorrow tomorrow in its absence.</b>

66
00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:52.750
<b>The object remains the same,</b>

67
00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:54.208
<b>the means remain the same,</b>

68
00:04:54.208 --> 00:04:56.291
<b>yet sometimes they bring joy,</b>

69
00:04:56.291 --> 00:04:58.208
<b>sometimes sorrow.</b>

70
00:04:58.208 --> 00:05:03.791
<b>This is a cycle that keeps turning.</b>

71
00:05:03.791 --> 00:05:05.500
<b>Similarly,</b>

72
00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:11.583
<b>for the eternal soul, </b>
<b>the greatest cause of suffering is</b>

73
00:05:11.583 --> 00:05:16.000
<b>the cycle of birth and death.</b>

74
00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:22.041
<b>This cycle sometimes lifts the soul towards joy,</b>

75
00:05:22.041 --> 00:05:26.166
<b>sometimes drops it towards sorrow.</b>

76
00:05:26.166 --> 00:05:27.083
<b>But</b>

77
00:05:27.083 --> 00:05:29.625
<b>how does this cycle operate?</b>

78
00:05:29.625 --> 00:05:33.083
<b>What is its power source?</b>

79
00:05:33.083 --> 00:05:36.125
<b>The results of our actions.</b>

80
00:05:36.125 --> 00:05:43.041
<b>Good results turn the wheel upward, </b>
<b>bad results turn it downward.</b>

81
00:05:43.041 --> 00:05:51.833
<b>The soul's endeavor is to stop this wheel,</b>
<b>to attain liberation.</b>

82
00:05:51.833 --> 00:05:55.291
<b>Now the question arises:</b>

83
00:05:55.291 --> 00:06:00.333
<b>how to stop this wheel?</b>

84
00:06:00.333 --> 00:06:02.416
<b>The answer is simple.</b>

85
00:06:02.416 --> 00:06:06.250
<b>By stopping its power source.</b>

86
00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:10.208
<b>And what is this power source?</b>

87
00:06:10.208 --> 00:06:13.041
<b>The results of our actions.</b>

88
00:06:13.041 --> 00:06:18.166
<b>So if the soul abandons expectation of results</b>

89
00:06:18.166 --> 00:06:22.958
<b>while righteously fulfilling its responsibilities,</b>

90
00:06:22.958 --> 00:06:27.250
<b>no result becomes good or bad.</b>

91
00:06:27.250 --> 00:06:30.333
<b>And if results aren't good or bad,</b>

92
00:06:30.333 --> 00:06:34.333
<b>the soul's wheel loses its power source.</b>

93
00:06:34.333 --> 00:06:36.583
<b>The wheel stops.</b>

94
00:06:36.583 --> 00:06:40.458
<b>This indeed is the soul's liberation.</b>

95
00:06:40.458 --> 00:06:45.541
<b>This is the essence of Nishkama Karma Yoga.</b>

96
00:06:45.541 --> 00:06:52.166
<b>"Act not thinking of good or bad results, </b>
<b>just perform your duty.</b>

97
00:06:52.166 --> 00:06:58.000
<b>Only by acting without expectation </b>
<b>will the soul find liberation."</b>

98
00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:00.250
<b>Simple to hear.</b>

99
00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:03.666
<b>Difficult to practice.</b>

100
00:07:03.666 --> 00:07:07.208
<b>But practice we must.</b>

101
00:07:11.958 --> 00:07:14.875
<b>As an elder in the family,</b>

102
00:07:14.875 --> 00:07:17.333
<b>it becomes your responsibility</b>

103
00:07:17.333 --> 00:07:21.916
<b>to establish a good example </b>
<b>for the younger ones.</b>

104
00:07:21.916 --> 00:07:24.791
<b>They will learn by watching you</b>

105
00:07:24.791 --> 00:07:28.666
<b>how to make decisions in any situation,</b>

106
00:07:28.666 --> 00:07:32.291
<b>how to handle circumstances.</b>

107
00:07:32.291 --> 00:07:33.416
<b>Therefore,</b>

108
00:07:33.416 --> 00:07:37.041
<b>if you want your children</b>

109
00:07:37.041 --> 00:07:37.833
<b>and</b>

110
00:07:37.833 --> 00:07:43.750
<b>dependent family members to</b>
<b>live a life free from sorrow,</b>

111
00:07:43.750 --> 00:07:50.208
<b>you must try to teach them </b>
<b>through your example</b>

112
00:07:50.208 --> 00:07:54.250
<b>how to live this life.</b>

113
00:07:54.250 --> 00:07:56.291
<b>Living life by renouncing attachments,</b>

114
00:07:56.291 --> 00:08:03.500
<b>rising above desires while performing </b>
<b>one's duties is the supreme way of living.</b>

115
00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:08.208
<b>If you live such a life with commitment,</b>

116
00:08:08.208 --> 00:08:17.125
<b>your family will surely be inspired to move </b>
<b>toward the true path of happiness.</b>

117
00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:23.625
<b>In this verse,</b>

118
00:08:23.625 --> 00:08:25.958
<b>there's a word...</b>

119
00:08:25.958 --> 00:08:28.125
<b>"Manishi"</b>

120
00:08:28.125 --> 00:08:32.125
<b>What does this word mean?</b>

121
00:08:32.125 --> 00:08:36.958
<b>Here it means a thoughtful person.</b>

122
00:08:36.958 --> 00:08:38.458
<b>Thoughtfulness</b>

123
00:08:38.458 --> 00:08:43.000
<b>means deep contemplation on any subject,</b>

124
00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:46.583
<b>understanding its essence.</b>

125
00:08:46.583 --> 00:08:53.166
<b>Through this Gita, I am teaching you </b>
<b>many life principles.</b>

126
00:08:53.166 --> 00:08:56.416
<b>Some principles will be new to you,</b>

127
00:08:56.416 --> 00:08:59.583
<b>some will be challenging.</b>

128
00:08:59.583 --> 00:09:02.125
<b>Understanding the essence of these principles,</b>

129
00:09:02.125 --> 00:09:05.041
<b>applying them correctly in life,</b>

130
00:09:05.041 --> 00:09:08.583
<b>is a process of continuous practice</b>

131
00:09:08.583 --> 00:09:14.625
<b>and only a Manishi, a thoughtful person, </b>
<b>can accomplish this.</b>

132
00:09:14.625 --> 00:09:16.416
<b>But</b>

133
00:09:16.416 --> 00:09:18.625
<b>how will you know</b>

134
00:09:18.625 --> 00:09:26.750
<b>if you're correctly applying </b>
<b>these principles in your life?</b>

135
00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:29.291
<b>This is very simple to know.</b>

136
00:09:29.291 --> 00:09:35.541
<b>The correct application of these principles</b>
<b>will lead you to a state of Aanmayam.</b>

137
00:09:35.541 --> 00:09:42.416
<b>A state where you don't experience</b>
<b>despair or sorrow,</b>

138
00:09:42.416 --> 00:09:48.333
<b>where negativity has no adverse effect on you,</b>

139
00:09:48.333 --> 00:09:54.458
<b>where you rise above all these afflictions.</b>

140
00:09:54.458 --> 00:09:58.916
<b>Isn't this the true purpose of action?</b>

141
00:09:58.916 --> 00:10:02.625
<b>To free life from afflictions.</b>

142
00:10:02.625 --> 00:10:04.375
<b>Continue your actions.</b>

143
00:10:04.375 --> 00:10:07.916
<b>Understand these principles with thoughtfulness</b>

144
00:10:07.916 --> 00:10:10.708
<b>and implement them in your life.</b>

